  "releaseNotes": "﻿### Added\n- The Python server (`credfeto-build-python`, MCP server `build-python`), a Native AOT dotnet tool: strict detection of `pyproject.toml` (`[project]` table) and `requirements*.txt` projects at the root, in `src/` and in `python.projects` directories, pip or uv (with `uv.lock`) with poetry, pipenv and pdm reported as unsupported, a `detect` tool (also offered when a repository has Python test files but no manifest), a non-recursive repository watch, `--self-test`, and the pointer and `linux-x64` tool packages; Core reads the `python` section of `.ai/commands.json` (`enabled`, `projects`, `timeoutMinutes`) on its own and adds the `Python` COVERAGE.md language (#58)\n- Python server jobs: `restore` into a per-project `.venv` (pip with `--only-binary :all:`, or `uv sync --frozen --no-build` with `uv.lock`, so no package code runs at install time and a package with no wheel fails), unpinned pytest and coverage with a note when the project does not declare them, a minimal `pyproject.toml` (or `requirements-dev.txt`) created for a test suite with no manifest, `test` (pytest with counts and failing test ids) and `lint` (flake8 and pylint as the global pre-commit hook runs them, plus pylint with super-linter's `.github/linters/.python-lint`), installing first when the manifests changed, and the shared `job_status` and `job_result` tools (#59)",
